+### Covered lanes
+
+Sections 1–3 MUST govern network Git acquisition in each of these lanes:
+
+- **Skillfile sources:** schema-2 `git`/`repository` sources, including
+  individual and collection selections ([Skillfile sources §1](skillfile-sources.md#1-acquisition-and-selection)),
+  and legacy skill acquisition from declared `git` URLs or configured network
+  source repositories ([core §5](core.md#5-project-manifests),
+  [manager §2](../profiles/manager.md#2-installation-lifecycle) and
+  [§4](../profiles/manager.md#4-install-scopes)).
+  This includes project, global and hybrid scopes.
+- **Skill dependencies and network development substitutions:**
+  `dependencies.skills` and the `git`/`ref` skill substitution form
+  ([core §4.4](core.md#44-dependencies), [core §5](core.md#5-project-manifests)).
+- **Profiles and their complete closure:** the Git root of `profile install`,
+  Git overlays and every Git requirement, including required skills and
+  transitive requirements ([manager §12.3](../profiles/manager.md#123-profile-lifecycle),
+  [environments §1](environments.md#1-environment-profiles-and-sources) and
+  [§6](environments.md#6-composition)).
+  Context packages containing `agent-context.json` and MCP declaration packages
+  containing `agent-mcp.json` are covered through this same closure
+  ([environments §2](environments.md#2-context-package-shape) and
+  [§2.2](environments.md#22-mcp-declaration-packages)); MCP declaration packages
+  are Git-only, not a separate transport exception.
+- **External skill build repositories:** `build_repositories` used by
+  `go-repository-v1`, including network development substitutions
+  ([core §4.2.2](core.md#422-schema-7-external-repositories-and-go-repository-v1) and
+  [§6.3](core.md#63-external-repository-source-identity-and-exact-lock),
+  [manager §11](../profiles/manager.md#11-external-repository-manager-profile)).
+  That lane's stricter endpoint and execution rules remain mandatory.
+
+Coverage follows the source through install, update/refresh, upgrade, repair
+and locked-snapshot reacquisition whenever the owning lane calls for network
+Git I/O; it does not make a read-only or store-only operation fetch. In
+particular, for a profile's declared SSH skill requirement with no applicable
+machine-policy entry, §2 requires one attempt at that declared SSH endpoint;
+canonical `host/path` identity does not authorize synthesizing an HTTPS URL.
+
+Local filesystem acquisition, `file:` sources and committed-HEAD local
+substitutions are not network endpoint selection and retain their own rules
+([core §§5–6](core.md#5-project-manifests),
+[Skillfile sources §2](skillfile-sources.md#2-physical-boundaries-and-admitted-local-inputs),
+[environments §1](environments.md#1-environment-profiles-and-sources)).
+Registry HTTP requests and MCP server connections are not Git package
+acquisition ([registry protocol](registry.md),
+[environments §2.2](environments.md#22-mcp-declaration-packages)); this protocol
+does not govern their transports or authorize installing a server. None of
+this list widens a lane's declaration grammar, ref rules or capabilities;
+logical `repository` declarations remain exclusive to new Skillfile sources.
+
